35,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Wow, the bills are all over the place! February was way more expensive than August. Also, some rooms are much colder than others because of the sunlight. This is going to be tricky!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The payment log shows a pattern of delays and confusion over the amounts. It seems the current system is causing friction. Also, installing sub-meters would be quite an expensive upfront investment for us.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Rin,,"I saw how another house does it, and it looks like a lot of work! They spent forty minutes just logging readings and doing math by hand. It seems really tedious!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"It turns out the ""carrying"" rumors have some merit. One person is using roughly four times the power of another, mostly thanks to a desktop and a heater. It's a bit of a gap, isn't it?","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Misaki,,The payment log shows that settlements are often late because people are confused or unhappy with the amounts. Even the cooler notice shows that some of us would rather suffer than argue over a pooled bill.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Shunichi, four times the power?! That's a huge difference! If some of us are freezing in the dark while others are cozy, we really need to talk about it now.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, that gap is significant. However, we must consider if the cost of fixing it is worth it. Sub-meters would be very expensive to install and maintain.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Ryuji, if it's too expensive to fix, maybe we can find a way that doesn't take forever to calculate? I don't want anyone spending their whole evening doing boring math!","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"Exactly. While Ryuji is worried about the cost of meters, we can't just ignore the fact that some of us are essentially subsidizing someone else's electricity bill. That's a recipe for resentment.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Shunichi, resentment is already here. The payment delays and the cooler notice prove that money is already damaging how we treat each other. We need a system that stops these silent conflicts.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mio,,"I totally agree with Misaki! I don't want us to be the kind of house where people are secretly annoyed. If we just split everything equally, will the people in the cold rooms feel it's unfair?","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"If we split equally, the disparity in usage and room temperature will likely continue to cause the friction Misaki mentioned. However, we cannot ignore the financial burden of a technical solution.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Rin,,"But if we use a fancy template to be perfectly fair, I found out it takes forever to key in every single invoice! Who is actually going to do all that work every month?","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, I'm sure you're not volunteering for the math, but spending ten minutes on a spreadsheet is a small price to pay to stop people from feeling cheated. Efficiency is great, but not at the cost of fairness.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Shunichi, fairness is important, but we should be careful that the process of achieving it doesn't become another source of tension. If the person managing the spreadsheet feels burdened, it just creates a new conflict.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Mio,,"I think we need to be honest about how we use the heat and power. If we just hide our habits to save money, we'll all be miserable by February! Let's find a balance.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"We need a solution that is sustainable over a full year. If we choose a system that is too complex or too expensive, we will likely return to the same confusion and delays we see in the logs.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Rin,,"I agree with Misaki! If the person doing the math gets tired and grumpy, it's not a happy house. We need something that's fair but super quick to do, or we'll just end up fighting again!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,Let's be realistic. We're adults; we can handle a bit of data entry if it means we stop subsidizing each other's lifestyles. A little effort now prevents a lot of bitterness later.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"We should prioritize a system that removes the need for constant reminders and questioning. If the process is transparent and agreed upon, we can stop the cycle of accusations and avoidance that's already happening.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
